      "math_academy_id": "e-12837",
      "problem": "Simplify the expression $-\\dfrac{1}{2}u  + \\dfrac{7}{8}u.$",
      "worked_solution": "We combine the like terms by adding the coefficients.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}u+\\frac{7}{8}u & = \\\\ (-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{7}{8})u & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to add the coefficients, we have to convert them to have the same denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{7}{8})u & = \\\\ (-\\frac{4}{8}+\\frac{7}{8})u & = \\\\ (\\frac{-4+7}{8})u & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{8}u & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the expression simplifies to $\\dfrac{3}{8}u.$",
